    <exercise xml:id="ex-points-on-the-axes-and-coordinate-planes">
        <!--<title></title>-->
        <stack label="stk-points-on-the-axes-and-coordinate-planes" source="stack/top/2-measurement-and-geometry/12-vectors-ii/01-vector-coordinates-in-two-and-three-dimensions/Points-on-the-axes-and-coordinate-planes.xml"/>
    </exercise>

    <exercises xml:id="exercises-coordinates-in-three-dimensions">
        <exercise xml:id="ex-write-coordinates">
            <statement>
                <p>Write the coordinates of each point.
                    <ol marker="(a)">
                        <li><p><m>4</m> units along the <m>x</m>-axis, <m>2</m> along the <m>y</m>-axis and <m>5</m> up.</p></li>
                        <li><p>On the <m>z</m>-axis, <m>3</m> units below <m>O</m>.</p></li>
                        <li><p>In the <m>xz</m>-plane, <m>2</m> along the <m>x</m>-axis and <m>6</m> up.</p></li>
                    </ol>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <answer><p>(a) <m>(4, 2, 5)</m> (b) <m>(0, 0, -3)</m> (c) <m>(2, 0, 6)</m></p></answer>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-cube-vertices">
            <statement><p>A cube of edge <m>6</m> has <m>O</m> as one vertex and three edges along the positive axes. List the coordinates of its eight vertices.</p></statement>
            <answer><p><m>(0, 0, 0)</m>, <m>(6, 0, 0)</m>, <m>(6, 6, 0)</m>, <m>(0, 6, 0)</m>, <m>(0, 0, 6)</m>, <m>(6, 0, 6)</m>, <m>(6, 6, 6)</m>, <m>(0, 6, 6)</m></p></answer>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-moves-between-points">
            <statement><p>Write the moves from <m>A(3, -2, 1)</m> to <m>B(-1, 4, 6)</m> as a column.</p></statement>
            <answer><p><m>\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ 6 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}</m></p></answer>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-water-tank-corners">
            <statement><p>A water tank at a school in Kisumu is a cuboid <m>3\,\text{m}</m> along the <m>x</m>-axis, <m>2\,\text{m}</m> along the <m>y</m>-axis and <m>1.5\,\text{m}</m> high. One bottom corner is at <m>(2, 1, 0)</m> and the tank lies in the positive directions from it. Give the coordinates of its four top corners.</p></statement>
            <answer><p><m>(2, 1, 1.5)</m>, <m>(5, 1, 1.5)</m>, <m>(5, 3, 1.5)</m>, <m>(2, 3, 1.5)</m></p></answer>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-point-from-midpoint">
            <statement><p><m>M(3, 1, 4)</m> is the midpoint of <m>AB</m>, and <m>A</m> is <m>(1, -2, 5)</m>. Find <m>B</m>.</p></statement>
            <answer><p><m>B(5, 4, 3)</m></p></answer>
            <solution><p>The moves from <m>A</m> to <m>M</m> are <m>\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}</m>. <m>B</m> is the same moves on from <m>M</m>: <m>(3 + 2, 1 + 3, 4 - 1) = (5, 4, 3)</m>.</p></solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-two-possible-cubes">
            <title>Challenge: Two Possible Cubes</title>
            <statement><p>A cube has vertices at <m>(3, 2, 0)</m>, <m>(8, 2, 0)</m> and <m>(3, 7, 0)</m>. Find the other five vertices.</p></statement>
            <hint><p>Is there only one such cube?</p></hint>
            <answer><p><m>(8, 7, 0)</m>, and either <m>(3, 2, 5)</m>, <m>(8, 2, 5)</m>, <m>(8, 7, 5)</m>, <m>(3, 7, 5)</m>, or the same four points with <m>z = -5</m>.</p></answer>
            <solution><p>The three given vertices lie in the <m>xy</m>-plane, and the edges from <m>(3, 2, 0)</m> are <m>5</m> long, so one face is the square with fourth corner <m>(8, 7, 0)</m>. The cube can stand on this square, with its other face at <m>z = 5</m>, or hang below it, with its other face at <m>z = -5</m>. Both cubes have edge <m>5</m>, so there are two answers.</p></solution>
        </exercise>
    </exercises>

    <axiom component="lesson-plan">
        <title>Differentiation</title>
        <table xml:id="table-differentiation-coordinates-in-three-dimensions">
            <title>Differentiation Strategies</title>
            <tabular halign="left" top="minor" bottom="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
                <row header="yes" bottom="medium"><cell>Learner Group</cell><cell>Strategy and Learning Experience</cell></row>
                <row><cell>Struggling Learners (Support)</cell><cell>Focus on activity parts (a) to (c) with a printed diagram of the room. Give a card: <q><m>x</m> along, <m>y</m> across, <m>z</m> up</q>. Assign <xref ref="ex-write-coordinates"/> and <xref ref="ex-cube-vertices"/>.</cell></row>
                <row><cell>On-Level Learners (Core)</cell><cell>Full activity plus all examples. Assign <xref ref="ex-write-coordinates"/> to <xref ref="ex-point-from-midpoint"/>.</cell></row>
                <row><cell>Advanced Learners (Challenge)</cell><cell>All exercises including <xref ref="ex-two-possible-cubes"/>. Extension: give the coordinates of the centre of the cube in <xref ref="ex-cube-vertices"/>. (Answer: <m>(3, 3, 3)</m>.)</cell></row>
            </tabular>
        </table>
    </axiom>

